<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>留学 on 编程那些事儿</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E7%95%99%E5%AD%A6/</link><description>Recent content in 留学 on 编程那些事儿</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:31:03 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E7%95%99%E5%AD%A6/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>留学适应</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/study/studying-abroad-adaptation/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/study/studying-abroad-adaptation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;留学最难的部分不是学业，是&lt;strong&gt;头三个月那种说不清的别扭&lt;/strong&gt;：能听懂课但听不懂玩笑，别人笑的时候你不知道该不该笑；食堂的菜吃两周就腻；室友周末有局但没叫你；生病了不知道去哪。这些事&lt;strong&gt;没人会主动问你&lt;/strong&gt;，而且用英语说出来本身就很难。&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>